# Secrets. This entry exists before any .env file does, which is the only
# ordering that guarantees a key can never be staged by accident.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.venv/
venv/

# Derived data. The raw upstream dump and the scratch files stay out; the
# built index does not.
#
# That is a reversal, and the reason is deployment. The index is derived and was
# excluded on principle, which meant a hosted instance rebuilt it on every cold
# start -- roughly three minutes of sustained CPU to download the corpus and
# encode 2,830 documents. The free host throttles for exactly that, and did.
#
# Committing 15MB of index removes the rebuild entirely, makes a cold start
# instant, and has a third benefit that only became clear once the artefacts
# were treated as a build output: the deployed app now serves the *same*
# clustering the documentation describes, including the model-written family
# descriptions, rather than whatever its own environment happened to produce.
# Written as artifacts/* rather than artifacts/: git does not descend into an
# excluded *directory*, so a negation beneath one can never match.
artifacts/*
!artifacts/index/
.cache/
.ruff_cache/
.pytest_cache/
*.log

# Model weights pulled from the Hub at runtime
.hf_home/

# OS
Thumbs.db
.DS_Store

# The rendered PDFs are tracked deliberately, alongside the markdown they are
# generated from. Both are small, and having them here means a reader does not
# need a working toolchain to read the report.
